  <data name="Welcome_Heading" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>iPhone app installer</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Welcome_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This installer puts FHZIPA INJECT on your computer, creates the shortcuts and registers the uninstaller. It does not touch the iPhone: installing apps on the device is done by the application itself, with your Apple account.</value>
  </data>
    <data name="Welcome_Info_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Installing apps on the iPhone is done by FHZIPA INJECT with your Apple ID, and the apps signed that way behave like the ones from the store: the signature expires in 7 days and the app has to be reinstalled; an iPhone usually accepts 3 signed apps per account; Apple can revoke the signature at any time; and installing modified apps violates the App Store Terms of Service.</value>
  </data>
    <data name="Welcome_Warning_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use this installer at your own risk. Make sure you have read and understood all the information above.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Welcome_Feature1_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Private</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Welcome_Feature1_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Your Apple account credentials stay on this computer.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Welcome_Feature2_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Light</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Welcome_Feature2_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The installer downloads no third-party drivers and does not change Windows.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Welcome_Feature3_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Reversible</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Welcome_Feature3_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Uninstaller, shortcuts and entry in Installed apps.</value>
  </data>
